-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  lex_comments.pcpp - Lexical: comments

  A line comment runs from two slashes to the end of its line; a block
  comment from slash-star to the first star-slash (BNF.md sec 9), over as
  many lines as it needs. A comment stands wherever a blank may: before
  code, after it, between two tokens, inside a call's parentheses. Block
  comments do not nest (lex_comments_err_nested), and two slashes are only
  text inside a string or a block comment. This header is a block comment
  too, so it never spells the two pairs.
*******************************************************************************/

module exe lex_comments;

/*
  @@test
    kind run
    expect
    | code
    | inline
    | // not a comment
    | between
    | after
    | [Heap] Allocs: 0, Frees: 0, Leaked: 0
  @@end
*/

// a line comment
/* a block comment
   over two lines */

begin
  println("code"); // after code
  println(/* inside */ "inline");
  println("// not a comment");
  /* one */ println("between"); /* two */
  /* a block comment holding // as text */ println("after");
end.
